\documentclass[11pt]{article}
\usepackage[margin=2.5cm]{geometry}

\title{Acquisition Report: The Lindqvist Bequest}
\author{Collections Committee, Vestfold Maritime Museum}
\date{August 2026}

\begin{document}
\maketitle

\section{The Bequest}
\label{sec:bequest}

The bequest comprises forty-one objects from the Lindqvist
family boathouse, together with a cash legacy earmarked for
conservation. The committee accepted the collection in May and
commissioned this report to steer the accession year.

\section{Provenance Research}
\label{sec:prov}

The archival work traces nineteen objects to the Bergen
registry of 1883. Two logbooks carry marginalia in Lindqvist's
own hand, and the Vienna registry cross-check confirmed the
export dates for the figurehead and the sternboard carvings.

\section{Conservation Assessment}
\label{sec:cons}

Condition scoring placed six objects in the urgent tier.
Solubility tests on the painted surfaces guided the choice of
consolidant, and the oak hull fragments require controlled
drying before they can join the display sequence of Section 4.

\section{Display Plan}
\label{sec:display}

The gallery narrative follows the archival work of Section 2,
and the condition summary in Section 3 sets the rotation
schedule, as flagged in Section~\ref{sec:cons}. Interpretation
panels will be drafted once the mount maker confirms the
bracket design for the heavier carvings.

\end{document}

